  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to check the panels render, and I haven't checked that the rule's query matches any documents. Its status was still \"pending\" right after creation.\n\n**Data:** The data view has a `timestamp` time field. The fields that matter for traffic are:\n- `response`, a string field with a `.keyword` subfield\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `clientip`\n- `machine.os`\n- `host`\n- `url`\n- `agent`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-b778edea Web logs overview\" has 5 panels. You can open it at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-b778edea-web-logs-overview-f73a00f54dc8.\n- **Total requests:** a single-number count of all requests.\n- **Requests over time:** an area chart of request counts by timestamp.\n- **Responses by status code:** a pie chart of the top 10 `response.keyword` values.\n- **Average bytes by extension:** a bar chart of average `bytes` for the top 10 file extensions.\n- **Top source countries:** a table of the top 10 `geo.src` values by request count.\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-b778edea 5xx spike\" (id `8807db1e-31cd-431e-87cf-0a065dbd062a`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute. It counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` over a 5-minute window, and fires when the count is above 10.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps may be older than the 5-minute window, in which case the rule won't fire until fresh data arrives.",
